<p>  Mining		     93.2   93.7   92.9   91.1   90.4</p>
<p>  Utilities		  89.1   87.5   86.8   89.3   91.3</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected April industrial production to rise 0.2 percent and estimated that April capacity use would be at a rate of 84.1 percent.</p>
<p>The Fed said strikes caused much of the April decline in output of autos and light trucks. Specifically, it said work stoppages accounted for more than half of a 6.8 percent decline in overall motor vehicle production last month.</p>
<p>Motor vehicle assemblies fell in April to a rate of 5.7 million a year for cars from 6.2 million in March. For light trucks the assembly rate fell to 5.2 million in April from 6.0 million in March.</p>
<p>Excluding motor vehicles and parts, April industrial output rose 0.3 percent after a 0.6 percent increase in March.</p>
<p>The Fed attributed much of last month's 2.0 percent rise in output of gas and electric utilities to relatively cool temperatures.</p>
